{"parentUuid":"2ed4881e-13b3-47e0-91f4-92f6948eea1c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNKe4QS8daaKt9crFqGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four *current* findings (the rest are stale, including the fork-bomb one I already fixed). Two are real bugs. Delegating per CLAUDE.md's orchestrator rule, starting with the two mediums:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_read_input_tokens":214660,"output_tokens":2370,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2370,"cache_read_input_tokens":214660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6173cd2d-e556-4c07-98cd-55fcf132cc18","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNKe45LZFM86jj9CMT11","requestRef":"e2afed6c-a016-40b8-9e91-7a2bd3babe02","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"46e0eddb-d566-47c0-b6df-520b95f378f0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:26:58.807Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"46e0eddb-d566-47c0-b6df-520b95f378f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNKe4QS8daaKt9crFqGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xmj5uJkXx4gb35fBrHsQpH","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix 489 transient-git finding","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished (branch fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints, PR entireio/entire-brain#489). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review.\n\nTHE FINDING (medium, current, id 01M5RK2YNSW8), verbatim:\n\"`partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` records every `localObjectType` error as \"unavailable\", including failures to run git at all (context cancellation, timeout, spawn or lock errors). Because the export is now fatal only when zero sessions are usable, a transient git failure silently drops sessions and republishes a shrunken corpus. Return runner/context errors as errors, and treat only a confirmed [object missing] as unavailable.\"\n\nIt is CORRECT and it is my bug. Context you need:\n- #489's whole point: a checkpoint whose commit no longer exists (squash-merge destroyed it) must not refuse the entire export. I replaced an all-or-nothing refusal with partition-and-warn via `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` in internal/cli/export.go, plus `unavailableSessionsAreFatal(usable, unavailable) bool { return usable == 0 && unavailable > 0 }`.\n- I over-corrected: I made EVERY probe failure mean \"the object is gone\". A ctx cancellation / git spawn failure / lock contention now silently shrinks the published corpus. That is worse than the refusal I removed.\n\nWHAT TO DO: distingua confirmed \"object does not exist\" from any other failure. Only the former is `unavailable`; everything else must propagate as an error and keep the export fatal. Find how git/`cat-file` reports a genuinely missing object in this codebase (there is existing precedent — look for how other call sites classify it) and classify on THAT, not on \"err != nil\". Beware: substring-matching git's stderr text is fragile; prefer an exit-code / typed / existing-helper route if one exists, and if you must match text, say so explicitly in a code comment and in your report.\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE verification, in this order:\n1. Targeted tests green: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your pattern>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`\n2. VERIFIED-BY-WEAKENING: for EACH new/changed guard, patch the production code so the guard SHOULD fail, run it, confirm it goes RED, then restore. A weakening that stays green means your test proves nothing — redo it. Check your patch applied (unique match) before trusting a green.\n3. Full gate: `mise run test:prepush` (go test ./... + gofmt -l -s + go vet). Redirect to a file, then grep the log for '^FAIL' and the recorded exit code — the task is one `set -e` script so only its first line echoes. Do NOT trust a bare exit 0 over an unread log.\n4. These existing tests MUST still pass — they encode why the old behaviour existed: TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache, TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude. The cache sweep learns retention from the selection and retention is what makes `privacy include` reversible.\n\nThen: `git add` only the files you changed, commit (conventional scoped subject; body explains WHY, no AI/Claude attribution footer of any kind), and `git push origin fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints`. Note the branch is based on #488 (fix/export-honours-session-tombstones) — do not rebase it, do not merge main.\n\nEnv notes: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3, which breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — if one fails, reproduce on main before believing it. Use rtk for shell commands. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT BACK caveman-ultra compressed, no prose padding: files+lines changed; how you classify \"missing\" and why that route; each weakening and red/green; prepush exit + FAIL count; the commit SHA; anything you could NOT verify. If you conclude the finding is wrong, say REFUTED with the evidence instead of changing code."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_read_input_tokens":214660,"output_tokens":2370,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2370,"cache_read_input_tokens":214660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xmj5uJkXx4gb35fBrHsQpH":{"description":"Fix 489 transient-git finding","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished (branch fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints, PR entireio/entire-brain#489). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review.\n\nTHE FINDING (medium, current, id 01M5RK2YNSW8), verbatim:\n\"`partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` records every `localObjectType` error as \"unavailable\", including failures to run git at all (context cancellation, timeout, spawn or lock errors). Because the export is now fatal only when zero sessions are usable, a transient git failure silently drops sessions and republishes a shrunken corpus. Return runner/context errors as errors, and treat only a confirmed [object missing] as unavailable.\"\n\nIt is CO