{"parentUuid":"06a3da05-c59f-43bc-b7e5-641dba1e3cb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLA4kMmpUY1QGftDjkc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Correcting the graph session — I gave them wrong information and it's material to their handoff:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":244255,"output_tokens":1322,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":225},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1322,"cache_read_input_tokens":244255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bee2cf75-d13b-41ba-9540-b7d40349ab66","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNLA4QXViQEddhAJ4nQu","requestRef":"a2505222-295d-4134-9096-ac2dc8706662","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"8100d781-39c7-428d-8955-f9f0476d45c8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:33:39.133Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"8100d781-39c7-428d-8955-f9f0476d45c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLA4kMmpUY1QGftDjkc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PUBiFsXqUfBRxv4Hvizt6y","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Correct the findings report: 8 real findings","message":"Correction to my handoff — brain findings are NOT zero, and you were right to push. My query was misaddressed.\n\nThe trail number in the gate's URL (entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/384) is REPO-scoped.\nI queried it as a project trail number (--trail 384 --project gh/entireio), which resolved a\ndependabot bump on cli and answered \"trail #384 has no open changes\". That reads exactly like a\nclean review. The correct form is --trail entire-brain/384, and the JSON carries trail.title and\ntrail.branch so you can confirm you are looking at the PR you think you are. Worth knowing for\nyour lane too if you built any graph counts the same way.\n\nREAL STATE: 8 open findings across 4 PRs; 4 of them CURRENT, the rest stale.\n  #477 3 open (1 current, low)    unbounded make([]byte, Content-Length) in readMCPFrame\n  #483 1 open (1 current, medium) the oversize skip misses the short-term delta path\n  #484 2 open (1 current, low)    probe FAILURES memoized, so a supporting provider is never re-asked\n  #489 2 open (1 current, medium) every localObjectType error read as \"object gone\"\nAll four are correct and all four are mine. The two mediums are real bugs, and #489's is the worst\nof them: I over-corrected a refusal into partition-and-warn and made a transient git failure\nsilently publish a shrunken corpus — worse than the refusal I removed.\n\nSo the reviews DO run on this repo. What I saw was my own bad query, not an absent pipeline. The\nstale ones include the fork-bomb finding I had already fixed, which is why freshness matters:\nquery --freshness any to see everything, then --freshness current for what is live.\n\nIN FLIGHT NOW, which changes your D2 timing: #489 and #483 are with subagents; #484 I have fixed\nmyself (cache only a definitive probe answer, and I also surfaced excluded_records in the emitted\nstaleness block — the stale medium finding was right that Unreliable is structurally empty in the\ncommon case, because it can only name paths the answer returned records for, and an ancestor store\nhas already dropped exactly those; without the excluded count beside it an incomplete answer is\nindistinguishable from a complete one. That is a change to the block your G1 contract covers, so\nflag it to them: five provider fields in, five out — I was re-emitting only four). Full gate\nrunning on #484 now.\n\nSo: brain is NOT final as of my last message. Give me until these four land before you freeze D2.\nI will send one more message when all four are pushed and green, with the final findings sweep.\n\nYour sequential-integration point is accepted and queued behind these fixes — fixing the findings\nfirst is the right order, since three of the four touch the export.go family that the integration\nbranch has to combine anyway. I will use your #381 recipe.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Correction to my handoff — brain findings are NOT…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":244255,"output_tokens":1322,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":225},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1322,"cache_read_input_tokens":244255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PUBiFsXqUfBRxv4Hvizt6y":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Correct the findings report: 8 real findings","message":"Correction to my handoff — brain findings are NOT zero, and you were right to push. My query was misaddressed.\n\nThe trail number in the gate's URL (entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/384) is REPO-scoped.\nI queried it as a project trail number (--trail 384 --project gh/entireio), which resolved a\ndependabot bump on cli and answered \"trail #384 has no open changes\". That reads exactly like a\nclean review. The correct form is --trail entire-brain/384, and the JSON carries trail.title and\ntrail.branch so you can confirm you are looking at the PR you think you are. Worth knowing for\nyour lane too if you built any graph counts the same way.\n\nREAL STATE: 8 open findings across 4 PRs; 4 of them CURRENT, the rest stale.\n  #477 3 open (1 current, low)    unbounded make([]byte, Content-Length) in readMCPFrame\n  #483 1 open (1 current, medium) the oversize skip misses the short-term delta path\n  #484 2 open (1 current, low)    probe FAILURES memoized, so a supporting provider is never re-asked\n  #489 2 open (1 current, medium) every localObjectType error read as \"object gone\"\nAll four are correct and all four are mine. The two mediums are real bugs, and #489's is the worst\nof them: I over-corrected a refusal into partition-and-warn and made a transient git failure\nsilently publish a shrunken corpus — worse than the refusal I removed.\n\nSo the reviews DO run on this repo. What I saw was my own bad query, not an absent pipeline. The\nstale ones include the fork-bomb finding I had already fixed, which is why freshness matters:\nquery --freshness any to see everything, then --freshness current for what is live.\n\nIN FLIGHT NOW, which changes your D2 timing: #489 and #483 are with subagents; #484 I have fixed\nmyself (cache only a definitive probe answer, and I also surfaced excluded_records in the emitted\nstaleness block — the stale medium finding was right that Unreliable is structurally empty in the\ncommon case, because it can only name paths the answer returned records for, and an ancestor store\nhas already dropped exactly those; without the excluded count beside it an incomplete answer is\nindistinguishable from a complete one. That is a change to the block your G1 contract covers, so\nflag it to them: five provider fields in, five out — I was re-emitting only four). Full gate\nrunning on #484 now.\n\nSo: brain is NOT final as of my last message. Give me until these four land before you freeze D2.\nI will send one more message when all four are pushed and green, with the final findings sweep.\n\nYour sequential-integration point is accepted and queued behind these fixes — fixing the findings\nfirst is the right order, since three of the four touch the export.go family that the integration\nbranch has to combine anyway. I will use your #381 recipe."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bee2cf75-d13b-41ba-9540-b7d40349ab66","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNLA4QXViQEddhAJ4nQu","requestRef":"a2505222-295d-4134-9096-ac2dc8706662","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"828aa533-dfdd-4190-ba9b-c063486ff44b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:33:55.780Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
