{"parentUuid":"b4bbbc27-35b6-4236-abfc-e23a106d8fbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNMvL5C75EbNECpxzsgh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BDDfNZpBP8u29e2nLdND2f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; git add internal/cli/graph_context_staleness_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(brief): assert excluded_records where an agent reads it, not only where it is built\n\nThe JSON-emission guard is containment based, so adding the field passed every\ntest in the file without asserting anything about it -- and dropping it again\nwould have passed too. The construction guard covers the struct; this covers\nthe layer an agent actually reads, which is the layer the field exists for.\n\nProved by weakening: retagging the field `json:\"-\"` turns this test red while\nthe construction guard stays green, so the two layers are independently held.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git push -q origin feat/brief-ancestor-staleness && echo pushed","description":"Commit and push the emission guard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":304820,"output_tokens":406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":51},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":304820,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BDDfNZpBP8u29e2nLdND2f":{"command":"cd /Users