{"parentUuid":"66afdf78-9c94-47a5-a75c-959db1e911d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNRBB5ESNK21hFDrxR8b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still running — 4 packages through, and `internal/cli` (the 232s–855s one) is the long pole. I'll report when it lands.\n\nMeanwhile I've closed out my side of the user-owned items by writing them up in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md` as sections 7 and 8, so they're in one place rather than scattered across this transcript.\n\nOn the stop hook's list, here's the honest split. **Mine, done:** all four review findings fixed and verified, the two main-conflicts plus #473's new one resolved, the full-order merge simulation clean against current main, and the combined tree compiling with zero vet findings. **Mine, in flight:** the combined-tree suite, running now.\n\n**Not mine, and I want to be straight about why** rather than claim them as finished:\n\n- **Approvals ×13** — you said explicitly to leave the PRs and stop asking. I won't.\n- **The #489 shrink guard** — I had the authority to decide this and I looked hard at it. I'm not deciding it because the question isn't technical: both technically-obvious fixes are actively wrong (one re-breaks #489 where it was needed, the other breaks `privacy exclude`), and what's left is whether an export that drops previously-published sessions should require explicit opt-in. That changes the CLI's contract, which is a product call, not an implementation one.\n- **Transcript mode** — spends your money on a corpus-wide re-distill.\n- **37 GB store delete** — irreversible.\n\nOne correction worth flagging: the first combined-tree run reported \"exit code 0\" in the task notification while the gate had actually failed — `mise` refused to trust a config in the scratch worktree, and the wrapper's trailing `echo` succeeded over it. That's the third time this session an exit code lied to me through a pipe or wrapper. The real status was `RECORDED_EXIT=1` with zero packages run, which is why I read the log rather than the notification."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":385383,"output_tokens":645,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":385383,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"898e2760-8169-4eae-81d0-4bea6d5ef396","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNRBAj8gASqvCjJUWWTj","requestRef":"470b722a-f3d0-42ad-89e3-4c2aac6af39e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"2051e54a-d5fe-4a85-85b2-433daea7336d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:39:33.986Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
