{"parentUuid":"a1269bbf-bb78-4596-bf0d-8d347c599b95","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14322741 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b349b68-6458-4b3e-8f97-382fd35f7623","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:44:45.855Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14322741 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"9b349b68-6458-4b3e-8f97-382fd35f7623","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNRaxjkCjMScq7rPewCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016vJm3cNbU5Mv5DCzie1jCm","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Integration result, patches, final SHAs","message":"All three things you need, and the integration passed.\n\n1. INTEGRATION RESULT — PASS. Draft PR **#493** (\"DO NOT MERGE: CI run of all 13 open brain PRs combined, in merge order\"), branch integration/brain-13-do-not-merge @ 9751b7d4, your #381 recipe. All 13 merge clean in order against main@20eb1207. On the combined tree locally: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 with **19 packages ok** + 3 no-test-files = 22 of 22 accounted for and zero `--- FAIL`; `gofmt -l -s .` silent; `go vet ./...` exit 0. I pushed it mainly for what I could NOT run — -race and Windows. CI owns both and no local run in this session reached them.\n\nYour warning earned its keep twice. Once as you meant it, and once from upstream drift: #490 (workspace extraction) and #491 landed on main mid-session, and #473 — clean two hours earlier — started conflicting in internal/cli/workspace.go. Pairwise-clean has a shelf life. Worth building into the handoff as a step, not a one-off check: re-run the sim immediately before the real merges.\n\n2. CONFLICT-RESOLUTION PATCHES — three, in\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/merge-patches/\n  pr473-resolution.patch   8266B  workspace.go + workspace_test.go\n  pr477-resolution.patch   1024B  lifecycle_ops.go\n  pr483-resolution.patch  14912B  history.go + history_oversize_tolerance_test.go\nEach is `git diff <merge>^2 <merge> -- <conflicted files>`, i.e. the branch's contribution as resolved relative to main's side, not the whole of what main dragged in. All three are COR-2268 extraction collisions. #473 is the one to read: loadWorkspaceManifest no longer exists, so the resolution keeps `pass++` and takes the manifest from workspaceStore(...).LoadManifest; deleting `pass++` turns its guard red, which is how I know the resolution kept the feature rather than merely compiling.\n\n3. FINAL 13 HEADS — confirmed final. Four moved beyond what I sent you, and #473 is a fifth you did not have:\n  #473 fix/distill-pipeline-v2                1f461e47   <-- NEW, main merged in\n  #474 fix/export-divergent-transcript        unchanged\n  #476 perf/history-terms-normalize-once      unchanged\n  #477 feat/mcp-surface-reachable             17f6bdc3\n  #478 perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint       unchanged\n  #479 perf/export-detail-fanout              unchanged\n  #480 fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap         unchanged\n  #481 perf/local-checkpoint-metadata         unchanged\n  #482 fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths          unchanged\n  #483 fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize   201fe6eb\n  #484 feat/brief-ancestor-staleness          8d3f4ce8\n  #488 fix/export-honours-session-tombstones  unchanged\n  #489 fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints  ce563535\n\nNothing else in flight on my side. Your D2 numbers stand — 2/2 main and 2/2 Explore going graph-first with the hook firing is the result that matters, and I agree grep-follows-for-exact-names is by design rather than a miss. I am not asking for a brain-side adoption number: it would need the harness's install step changed, that is a measurement campaign rather than a handoff item, and the brain PRs are gated on Approvals anyway.\n\nOne last thing for the page, since it is the only open item that is not an approval: the #489 partial-shrink guard is a CLI-contract question, not a defect — should an export that would drop previously-published sessions require explicit opt-in, or keep publishing with a warning? Written up for Suhaan as section 7 of devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md and recorded in brain at architecture.export.constraint. #489 should not wait on it.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"All three things you need, and the integration pa…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":400244,"output_tokens":1563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":400244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016vJm3cNbU5Mv5DCzie1jCm":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Integration result, patches, final SHAs","message":"All three things you need, and the integration passed.\n\n1. INTEGRATION RESULT — PASS. Draft PR **#493** (\"DO NOT MERGE: CI run of all 13 open brain PRs combined, in merge order\"), branch integration/brain-13-do-not-merge @ 9751b7d4, your #381 recipe. All 13 merge clean in order against main@20eb1207. On the combined tree locally: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 with **19 packages ok** + 3 no-test-files = 22 of 22 accounted for and zero `--- FAIL`; `gofmt -l -s .` silent; `go vet ./...` exit 0. I pushed it mainly for what I could NOT run — -race and Windows. CI owns both and no local run in this session reached them.\n\nYour warning earned its keep twice. Once as you meant it, and once from upstream drift: #490 (workspace extraction) and #491 landed on main mid-session, and #473 — clean two hours earlier — started conflicting in internal/cli/workspace.go. Pairwise-clean has a shelf life. Worth building into the handoff as a step, not a one-off check: re-run the sim immediately before the real merges.\n\n2. CONFLICT-RESOLUTION PATCHES — three, in\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/merge-patches/\n  pr473-resolution.patch   8266B  workspace.go + workspace_test.go\n  pr477-resolution.patch   1024B  lifecycle_ops.go\n  pr483-resolution.patch  14912B  history.go + history_oversize_tolerance_test.go\nEach is `git diff <merge>^2 <merge> -- <conflicted files>`, i.e. the branch's contribution as resolved relative to main's side, not the whole of what main dragged in. All three are COR-2268 extraction collisions. #473 is the one to read: loadWorkspaceManifest no longer exists, so the resolution keeps `pass++` and takes the manifest from workspaceStore(...).LoadManifest; deleting `pass++` turns its guard red, which is how I know the resolution kept the feature rather than merely compiling.\n\n3. FINAL 13 HEADS — confirmed final. Four moved beyond what I sent you, and #473 is a fifth you did not have:\n  #473 fix/distill-pipeline-v2                1f461e47   <-- NEW, main merged in\n  #474 fix/export-divergent-transcript        unchanged\n  #476 perf/history-terms-normalize-once      unchanged\n  #477 feat/mcp-surface-reachable             17f6bdc3\n  #478 perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint       unchanged\n  #479 perf/export-detail-fanout              unchanged\n  #480 fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap         unchanged\n  #481 perf/local-checkpoint-metadata         unchanged\n  #482 fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths          unchanged\n  #483 fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize   201fe6eb\n  #484 feat/brief-ancestor-staleness          8d3f4ce8\n  #488 fix/export-honours-session-tombstones  unchanged\n  #489 fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints  ce563535\n\nNothing else in flight on my side. Your D2 numbers stand — 2/2 main and 2/2 Explore going graph-first with the hook firing is the result that matters, and I agree grep-follows-for-exact-names is by design rather than a miss. I am not asking for a brain-side adoption number: it would need the harness's install step changed, that is a measurement campaign rather than a handoff item, and the brain PRs are gated on Approvals anyway.\n\nOne last thing for the page, since it is the only open item that is not an approval: the #489 partial-shrink guard is a CLI-contract question, not a defect — should an export that would drop previously-published sessions require explicit opt-in, or keep publishing with a warning? Written up for Suhaan as section 7 of devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md and recorded in brain at architecture.export.constraint. #489 should not wait on it."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6e8b601d-fcdf-4ec9-9475-84610560d762","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNRaxCVGwCGDXU3g2cgZ","requestRef":"ac5cc2ce-5da7-453f-9a05-f65c07db4bab","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"12ab5cc5-3702-4bdc-8511-f365efd589b5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:45:06.965Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
