{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"92c03e5b-c8e8-4eda-8c66-ec60a645aea7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:50:45.308Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"24017389debf7cd8bde5028ecf29c4ee6405c6fe767d12c483cd96a0e96b3788","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","context-1m-2025-08-07","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"358dff7e-61eb-41a6-8ce2-d86d662eb172","keep":732,"tail":["57279abddf9334df9150eac0e28f6552718357922c2002c36110275231a9984a","3e6d19d9ee833a12cfb63a0772c9715d4c9e127ac11145b28a0433ae6e4e8d9f","99dc1151f121e82a3a2e457b66bb66179fc4e6ea20b6bfeb8993fd9f9ba9339c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",734,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"75252152007e753f4039256ea1affe5505643af802b47deacf317e97b2d07e50"}
{"parentUuid":"6df19df0-c113-4c7e-a09d-6ef919140726","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14293796 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b5599676-e06d-4458-a590-c882c776a2db","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:50:45.274Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14293796 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"b5599676-e06d-4458-a590-c882c776a2db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNS3TCV6SAHBMpTfzpna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I was wrong to hand you that decision, and I've closed it instead.**\n\nMy reason for declining was that treating \"promisor remote exists\" as \"might be fetchable\" would re-break #489 exactly where it was needed. That's false, and the agent's own report contained the clue I underweighted — its vanished-checkpoint fixture \"never reaches the git probe at all.\" There are two separate paths:\n\n- A checkpoint whose **commit** was destroyed has no snapshot entry and no chunks, so it's classified **from data** and git is never consulted. That's #489's real target.\n- The git probe only ever sees a chunk the snapshot *does* name whose bytes are absent locally — which is precisely the fetchable case.\n\nSo tightening the probe branch costs #489 nothing. The fix: if the source repo has a promisor remote, an absent object isn't definitive and the export fails rather than silently dropping the session. Full clones are untouched — absent there is absent for good, and they still partition.\n\nThe detection detail is where my own notes paid off: `cli`'s promisor remote is named **by URL** (`remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor`) and `extensions.partialclone` isn't set at all. A detector written against `remote.origin.promisor` — the obvious thing to write — would pass every fake-runner test and miss the one repository the guard exists for. So I matched by suffix across all remotes and pinned it against real git.\n\nFour weakenings, and the third is the one worth noting: narrowing the pattern to `origin` turns the **real-git** test red while the fake-runner tests stay **green**. That's not a passing test, it's a demonstration that the fakes could never have caught it. Two earlier weakening attempts were build failures from my own shell escaping — those prove nothing, and I redid both.\n\nGate running. When it passes: #489 gets a new SHA, #493 needs re-pushing since it now holds a stale #489, and `DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md` §7 gets rewritten from a decision you owe me into a closed item. That leaves you **Approvals**, **transcript mode** (your money), and the **37 GB delete** (irreversible) — and I'll stop claiming the first one is something I can finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":429639,"output_tokens":737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":429639,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d4b33a0b-8a09-48b2-bb61-eb43b404c898","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNS3Stsxk7EUEC5sq1Ud","requestRef":"92c03e5b-c8e8-4eda-8c66-ec60a645aea7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"168a1dac-1b22-4e7a-a0fb-7b1c042089fc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:50:55.796Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
