tBinary, TestReadMCPFrameRefusesAnOversizedContentLength, TestReadMCPFrameRefusesANegativeContentLength, TestReadMCPFrameAcceptsALengthAtTheCap, TestReadMCPFrameKeepsAZeroLengthBodyLegal, TestReadMCPFrameStillReadsAnOrdinaryFrame, TestReadMCPFrameStillReportsAMissingContentLength, TestMCPProbeRefusesAnOversizedFrameInsteadOfAllocatingIt, TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults. Run with -v and confirm the names appear.\n3. PROVE THE RESOLUTION KEPT THE WIRING: delete the `doctorMCPSurfaceCheck(...)` call from `brainDoctorReadOnlyReport`, confirm `--- FAIL: TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck`, restore. A `[build failed]` is NOT a red; keep the package compiling and verify your patch applied as a unique match first.\n4. Full gate: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m mise run test:prepush > /tmp/g477.log 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> /tmp/g477.log`. The `-timeout` is REQUIRED: internal/cli is 232s idle but 805-855s under parallel load against go test's 10m default, and other agents are running suites right now. Grep the log for `--- FAIL` and the recorded EXIT; never trust a bare exit code over an unread log.\n\nThen commit (conventional subject; body states what main extracted, what you kept, the weakening; NO AI/Claude attribution footer) and `git push origin feat/mcp-surface-reachable`.\n\nEnv: FORCE_COLOR=3 is set here and fails colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing one. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT caveman-ultra compressed: conflicted hunks + resolution; renames followed in tests; the weakening and its exact `--- FAIL` line; gate EXIT + FAIL count + package count; commit SHA; anything unverified.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85/tasks/a4bf618f67f591344.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c9f95697-a3af-442b-93f9-0161b767c1c1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brai