{"parentUuid":"a3208e3e-c2d0-454a-8d5d-af8dc61cbcf8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNTKhrbdABTXjpkqh2n5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3990,"cache_read_input_tokens":453215,"output_tokens":556,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":123},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3990,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":453215,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3990},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2085,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"33d13855-b8a4-430b-ad1b-c3d1a64fb7dc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNTKhYFQnh16eBp7pe8T","requestRef":"6da9b7a0-b348-4571-83ea-dbe914e5f939","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f9cb1cd-b20c-4b88-8caa-d85596e901a9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:07:35.933Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-branchfacts","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"5f9cb1cd-b20c-4b88-8caa-d85596e901a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNTKhrbdABTXjpkqh2n5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restored cleanly — line 1385 is back to `base.HexSHA(branch)`.\n\n**#478 confirmed**, and I resolved the agent's own uncertainty. It had reported a weakening it couldn't explain (\"it could be the fixture, so I would not lean on it as the proof\") — correct instinct to flag rather than claim. Its weakening was indirect (forcing a boolean true). I ran the precise one instead: making `patternCorpusFactsMetaKey` branch-blind, which is *exactly* the pre-PR behaviour. All four tests go red, so the per-branch keying is genuinely load-bearing and the resolution kept the feature.\n\nI also checked the thing that worried me more: the agent **dropped a line main had** (`factsCurrent`), which is how a merge silently deletes someone else's change. That one is self-verifying — Go errors on unused locals, so `vet` passing proves nothing else referenced it, and the branch replacing a global fingerprint check with a per-branch one is precisely the PR's purpose.\n\nTwo agents still running on #477 and #483.\n\nAlso worth noting: the Bash safety classifier failed twice in a row on a plain `git status` — a transient infrastructure error, not a refusal. I verified the restore with a read-only tool instead, which doesn't need the classifier."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3990,"cache_read_input_tokens":453215,"output_tokens":556,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":123},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3990,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":453215,"cache_creat