{"parentUuid":"e9edbe1e-7a34-415d-9189-0ffe6a49bdd9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNTbAmmbSGAHDB1WFAvy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V7VEUwA26Jd6a55oLSfLR1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/RESUME-483-UNCOMMITTED.md","content":"# UNFINISHED: #483 has a resolved-but-uncommitted merge (2026-10-25)\n\n**One command finishes this.** The work is done and verified; only the commit and push are\nmissing, because the Bash safety classifier began erroring (no verdict) and never recovered.\nThat is an infrastructure failure, not a permission decision and not a problem with the code.\n\n## State\n\nWorktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize`, branch\n`fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize` (PR entireio/entire-brain#483).\n\n- `git merge origin/main` is IN PROGRESS. `MERGE_HEAD` = `ab575071` (main at the time).\n  Note `.git` here is a *file*, so `MERGE_HEAD` lives at\n  `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/.git/worktrees/brain-history-oversize/MERGE_HEAD`.\n- The conflict was 3 hunks in `internal/cli/history.go`, all in the transcript size checks\n  (`digestHistorySessionInventoryFile` ×2, `readHistorySessionInventoryFile` ×1).\n- **Resolved, not staged.** `internal/cli/history.go` is edited; `transcript_store.go`\n  auto-merged.\n\n## The resolution, and why it is right\n\nmain's COR-2268 series extracted the read bounds into `internal/cli/internal/base`, which\n`history.go` imports under the alias **`clibase`** (other files in the package use `base` —\ndo not \"fix\" that, it is per-file). main inlined the refusal; this branch uses a sentinel.\n\nResolution keeps the branch's sentinel and adopts main's alias, e.g. at history.go:1433:\n\n```go\nif file.Size > clibase.MaxDocumentTranscriptBytes {\n    return \"\", historyTranscriptTooLargeError(file.Rel)\n}\n```\n\nThat is the point of the PR: one transcript too large to read must be SKIPPED, not refuse the\nwhole history index. Taking main's side here would compile, pass most things, and silently\ndelete the feature.\n\n## Verified before the classifier failed\n\n- `go vet ./internal/cli/` exit 0.\n- All 8 required tests pass **by name**: `TestHistoryIndexSkipsAnOversizeTranscriptAndIndexesTheRest`,\n  `TestOversizeTranscriptIsSkippedByEveryInventoryReader`,\n  `TestStoreSizeRefusalClassifiesAsTheSkippableOversizeError`,\n  `TestShortTermDeltaSkipsAnOversizeTranscriptAndIndexesTheRest`,\n  `TestShortTermDeltaRefusesEveryBoundBreachExceptTheTranscriptCap`,\n  `TestShortTermDeltaOversizeTranscriptIsRecordedNotRefused`,\n  `TestShortTermDeltaNonTranscriptBoundBreachPreservesPriorOverlay`,\n  `TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults`.\n- Weakening: `if false && errors.Is(digestErr, errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge)` at the identity\n  reader turned two tests red (`--- FAIL`, compiled, so a real red rather than a build\n  failure), then restored.\n- Full gate `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m mise run test:prepush`: EXIT=0, zero `--- FAIL`,\n  20 `ok` packages. Log `/tmp/g483.log`.\n- I independently re-read history.go:1428-1452 and confirmed the resolution shape above and\n  that no conflict markers remain.\n\n## To finish\n\n```sh\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize\ngit status --porcelain              # expect history.go, plus anything else unmerged\ngit add internal/cli/history.go     # add any other unmerged paths status shows\ngit commit -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge origin/main into fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\n\nmain's COR-2268 series extracted the read bounds into internal/cli/internal/base, which\nhistory.go imports as clibase, and inlined the size refusal on the three lines this branch\nrewrites. Resolved toward this branch's sentinel -- historyTranscriptTooLargeError, so one\noversize transcript is skipped rather than refusing the whole index -- while adopting main's\nalias at all three sites.\n\nRe-proved rather than assumed: the eight guards pass by name, and disabling the sentinel skip\nin the identity reader turns two of them red.\nMSG\ngit push origin fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\n```\n\n## Then\n\n1. `#493` (the DO-NOT-MERGE integration PR) holds a stale `#483` and a stale `#489`. Re-run\n   the sequential simulation from current `main` and re-push it.\n2. Expect more conflicts: main is taking the COR-2268 extraction series (#490 workspace,\n   #491 semantic, #492 patterns) roughly every 25 minutes, and each extraction collides with\n   whichever branch touches the same file. A merge simulation is a step to run immediately\n   before the real merges, never a result to quote from earlier.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":483179,"output_tokens":2378,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2378,"cache_read_input_tokens":483179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01V7VEUwA26Jd6a55oLSfLR1":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/RESUME-483-UNCOMMITTED.md","content":"# UNFINISHED: #483 has a resolved-but-uncommitted merge (2026-10-25)\n\n**One command finishes this.** The work is done and verified; only the commit and push are\nmissing, because the Bash safety classifier began erroring (no verdict) and never recovered.\nThat is an infrastructure failure, not a permission decision and not a problem with the code.\n\n## State\n\nWorktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv/