{"parentUuid":"5e40532a-6037-4d87-9c92-f5b933ef7f66","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNU3NJ334o9X42YZWV7M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MhrJyKog7DeaMkenakws5b","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Final brain SHAs; 483 pushed","message":"Final brain heads — #483 is now pushed, so nothing is pending on my side. The safety classifier had been returning no verdict for about eleven consecutive calls, which is why this is late; it has recovered.\n\nTHE 13, final:\n  #473 fix/distill-pipeline-v2                 1f461e47\n  #474 fix/export-divergent-transcript         unchanged\n  #476 perf/history-terms-normalize-once       unchanged\n  #477 feat/mcp-surface-reachable              906e8ad3\n  #478 perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint        67d3321c\n  #479 perf/export-detail-fanout               unchanged   (ancestor of #481)\n  #480 fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap          unchanged\n  #481 perf/local-checkpoint-metadata          unchanged\n  #482 fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths           unchanged\n  #483 fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize    fbc2946a    <-- NEW, was 201fe6eb\n  #484 feat/brief-ancestor-staleness           8d3f4ce8\n  #488 fix/export-honours-session-tombstones   unchanged   (ancestor of #489)\n  #489 fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints   c0117710\n\nRe-simulated against main@ab575071: all 13 merge CLEAN in the same order. The combined-tree suite is running now and I will send its result; the previous pass was against main@20eb1207 with older #483 and #489, so treat #493's current result as superseded until I confirm.\n\n#483's merge resolution, for the patch set: main's COR-2268 extraction moved the read bounds into internal/cli/internal/base, which history.go imports as `clibase` (other files in the package use `base` — that is per-file, not a mistake to normalise). Kept the branch's `historyTranscriptTooLargeError` sentinel at all three size checks and adopted main's alias. Verified: vet clean, eight guards passing by name, and disabling the sentinel skip in the identity reader turns two of them red. I re-read all three hunks myself before committing.\n\nTwo things unchanged from my last message and worth keeping on the page:\n- Two stacks only. I checked whether #477 and #478 were a hidden third — they conflicted in the same file over the same per-branch fact code — and `merge-base --is-ancestor` says #478 is NOT an ancestor of #477.\n- Main is still taking the COR-2268 series (#490, #491, #492) roughly every 25 minutes, and it invalidated a clean full-order simulation twice in one session with none of my branches changing. \"All 13 merge clean\" is only true of a named main SHA, so the re-simulation step you put on the page is load-bearing, not ceremony.\n\nAlso, in case they are useful beside the three you copied: #477, #478 and #483 each needed a SECOND main-merge after that earlier set, so there are three further resolutions on those branches that are not in ~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/brain-patches/.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Final brain heads — #483 is now pushed, so nothin…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":744,"cache_read_input_tokens":499735,"output_tokens":1135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":744,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1135,"cache_read_input_tokens":499735,"cache_creation_input_tokens":744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":744},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback