{"parentUuid":"fe0c5179-51cd-47d6-ad3c-0e1a4e867b3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPEsBCVvYZAtrdsHtcX3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013jk47hw3pz8zPH53cXY2yV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"pr493.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nadd = \"\"\"\n## Refreshed against `main@a4942dd9` (2026-10-25) — and it found a real defect\n\n`#494` (workspace-families extraction) and `#495` landed, re-conflicting `#477` and `#478` in\n`internal/cli/pattern_corpus.go`: `main` had moved `corpusMeta` into `patterncore` as\n`CorpusMeta`. Both resolved by keeping the branch's per-branch-fingerprint behaviour and\nadopting `main`'s name, proved by restoring the global fingerprint and taking a named\n`--- FAIL: TestFactOnOneBranchDoesNotReindexAnotherBranchsSessions` with the package still\ncompiling.\n\nRe-running the simulation also exposed something a per-PR gate could never show: **`#477`\ncontained the whole of `#478`** — `pattern_corpus.go` +92 and\n`pattern_corpus_branch_facts_test.go` +174, identical blob SHAs, added under a commit message\nabout an unrelated stderr-sink fix. `git merge-base --is-ancestor` had already told me the two\nwere not stacked, which is true of their *history* and says nothing about their *content*.\n`#477` is now cut back to its own four files; `#478` carries its feature alone, and this tree\nholds `patternCorpusFactsMetaKey` exactly once.\n\nEvery other branch was audited the same way (`git diff --stat origin/main...<branch>` read\nagainst its subject). No other PR carries out-of-subject content: `#481` showing `#479`'s\nfiles and `#489` showing `#488`'s are the two declared stacks, and `#480`'s eight extra test\nfiles are one fake-runner fixture key moved to a shared helper.\n\nAll thirteen merge clean in order on `a4942dd9`.\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"## Refreshed against\"\nif marker in s:\n    s = s[:s.index(marker)] + add.lstrip(\"\\n\")\nelse:\n    # insert before the CI section if present, else append\n    anchor = \"## CI closed the gap\"\n    s = (s[:s.index(anchor)] + add.lstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + s[s.index(anchor):]) if anchor in s else s + add\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"ok\", len(s))\nPY\ngh pr edit 493 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file pr493.md 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Update the 493 PR body with the refresh and defect found"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":151629,"output_tokens":968,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":968,"cache_read_input_tokens":151629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013jk47hw3pz8zPH53cXY2yV":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"pr493.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nadd = \"\"\"\n## Refreshed against `main@a4942dd9` (2026-10-25) — and it found a real defect\n\n`#494` (workspace-families extraction) and `#495` landed, re-conflicting `#477` and `#478` in\n`internal/cli/pattern_corpus.go`: `main` had moved `corpusMeta` into `patterncore` as\n`CorpusMeta`. Both resolved by keeping the branch's per-branch-fingerprint behaviour and\nadopting `main`'s name, proved by restoring the global fingerprint and taking a named\n`--- FAIL: TestFactOnOneBranchDoesNotReindexAnotherBranchsSessions` with the package still\ncompiling.\n\nRe-running the simulation also exposed something a per-PR gate could never show: **`#477`\ncontained the whole of `#478`** — `pattern_corpus.go` +92 and\n`pattern_corpus_branch_facts_test.go` +174, identical blob SHAs, added under a commit message\nabout an unrelated stderr-sink fix. `git merge-base --is-ancestor` had already told me the two\nwere not stacked, which is true of their *history* and says nothing about their *content*.\n`#477` is now cut back to its own four files; `#478` carries its feature alone, and this tree\nholds `patternCorpusFactsMetaKey` exactly once.\n\nEvery other branch was audited the same way (`git diff --stat origin/main...<branch>` read\nagainst its subject). No other PR carries out-of-subject content: `#481` showing `#479`'s\nfiles and `#489` showing `#488`'s are the two declared stacks, and `#480`'s eight extra test\nfiles are one fake-runner fixture key moved to a shared helper.\n\nAll thirteen merge clean in order on `a4942dd9`.\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"## Refreshed against\"\nif marker in s:\n    s = s[:s.index(marker)] + add.lstrip(\"\\n\")\nelse:\n    # insert before the CI section if present, else append\n    anchor = \"## CI closed the gap\"\n    s = (s[:s.index(anchor)] + add.lstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + s[s.index(anchor):]) if anchor in s else s + add\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"ok\", len(s))\nPY\ngh pr edit 493 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file pr493.md 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Update the 493 PR body with the refresh and defect found"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"abff9ac7-0a4b-4260-ab3c-c7cb560e4c95","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPEsArR5gj3uLWr1oTx2","requestRef":"e0d13f41-8ef6-462d-a624-d46273db5d55","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"734ae87e-da3c-44ac-93ff-98a244ee3978","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:04:59.323Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_