still's --jobs goroutines). If the sharing claim does not hold, say so with the evidence and stop — do not invent a fix.\n\nIf real, fix it: guard Write with a sync.Mutex. Keep the change minimal and in the surrounding file's style (match its comment density and naming; the file uses substantial explanatory comments). Add a test that actually fails without the mutex — a concurrent-writer test run under `-race`.\n\nMANDATORY VERIFICATION, report each command and its real result:\n1. `go build ./...` exit 0.\n2. Your new test RED without the fix: remove the mutex lock, run the test with `-race`, and confirm a NAMED `--- FAIL` or a race report naming watchLogPrefixWriter. CRITICAL: `[build failed]` is NOT a red — it greps as `^FAIL` but the test never ran. Keep the package compiling (use `_ = x` for orphaned vars) and grep for `--- FAIL` plus `WARNING: DATA RACE`. Report the exact test name.\n3. Restore the fix; test GREEN under `-race`.\n4. `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your tests>|TestWatch' -count=1 -race` green.\n5. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` silent (note: gofmt on PATH is an older Go; use the GOROOT one).\n6. `go vet ./...` exit 0 — capture the status directly, never through a pipe (`cmd > log 2>&1; echo $?`), because piping to head reports head's status.\n7. Commit (NO AI attribution footer, no Co-Authored-By — repo rule) and push to origin fix/distill-pipeline-v2. Report the new head SHA.\n8. Resolve the finding: `entire trail finding resolve --trail entire-brain/384 --finding 01M5RS21DZA20NW7JMZVAVG1FT --json` (check `entire trail finding resolve --help` for exact flag names first). If it 404s, the local `entire` binary is stale — report that, don't guess.\n\nNote: `internal/cli` is a huge package (232s idle, 805s+ under load) vs go test's 10m default, so always pass GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m. Scope your -run to your tests, don't run the whole package.\n\nReport: race confirmed? (evidence), what you changed, the exact weakening red (