{"parentUuid":"c6b8f02a-3f02-4d51-be4a-89cd2cb3e838","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"48505276-424b-4311-9824-04b880049694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PSDji7wPf8Ka81rfEUnJnW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: af35f1ec41f89ea32 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'af35f1ec41f89ea32', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85/tasks/af35f1ec41f89ea32.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"5a2f69f3-ab4e-4b63-aa13-67d087c709fc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:17:02.393Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"af35f1ec41f89ea32","description":"Fix PR 473 watch writer race","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","prompt":"Fix one agent-review finding in the entire-brain repo. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-dp2 (branch fix/distill-pipeline-v2, PR #473). Do not touch any other worktree or branch.\n\nCAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED OUTPUT. Use rtk (token-saving CLI proxy) for git/shell where it applies. Your tool output never reaches me — only your final report — so make the report dense and factual.\n\nTHE FINDING (trail entire-brain/384, id 01M5RS21DZA20NW7JMZVAVG1FT, severity low), verbatim:\n\"`watchLogPrefixWriter.Write` mutates `midLine` and builds the prefix with no mutex. `watchStepCommand` now hands this one writer to distill/refresh/seed as both stdout and stderr, and distill runs concurrent goroutines (`--jobs`) that can write warnings directly to it. That is a data race and can interleave or mis-stamp lines. Guard `Write` with a `sync.Mutex`.\"\n\nTreat the finding as a hypothesis to verify, not a fact. First confirm the race is real by reading the code: find watchLogPrefixWriter (likely internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go), confirm Write mutates shared state, and confirm via the call path that one writer instance is genuinely shared across concurrent writers (watchStepCommand -> distill/refresh/seed, distill's --jobs goroutines). If the sharing claim does not hold, say so with the evidence and stop — do not invent a fix.\n\nIf real, fix it: guard Write with a sync.Mutex. Keep the change minimal and in the surrounding file's style (match its comment density and naming; the file uses substantial explanatory comments). Add a test that actually fails without the mutex — a concurrent-writer test run under `-race`.\n\nMANDATORY VERIFICATION, report each command and its real result:\n1. `go build ./...` exit 0.\n2. Your new test RED without the fix: remove the mutex lock, run the test with `-race`, and confirm a NAMED `--- FAIL` or a race report naming watchLogPrefixWriter. CRITICAL: `[build failed]` is NOT a red — it greps as `^FAIL` but the test never ran. Keep the package compiling (use `_ = x` for orphaned vars) and grep for `--- FAIL` plus `WARNING: DATA RACE`. Report the exact test name.\n3. Restore the fix; test GREEN under `-race`.\n4. `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your tests>|TestWatch' -count=1 -race` green.\n5. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` silent (note: gofmt on PATH is an older Go; use the GOROOT one).\n6. `go vet ./...` exit 0 — capture the status directly, never through a pipe (`cmd > log 2>&1; echo $?`), because piping to head reports head's status.\n7. Commit (NO AI attribution footer, no Co-Authored-By — repo rule) and push to origin fix/distill-pipeline-v2. Report the new head SHA.\n8. Resolve the finding: `entire trail finding resolve --trail entire-brain/384 --finding 01M5RS21DZA20NW7JMZVAVG1FT --json` (check `entire trail finding resolve --help` for exact flag names first). If it 404s, the local `entire` binary is stale — report that, don't guess.\n\nNote: `internal/cli` is a huge package (232s idle, 805s+ under load) vs go test's 10m default, so always pass GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m. Scope your -run to your tests, don't run the whole package.\n\nReport: race confirmed? (evidence), what you changed, the exact weakening red (test name + race report presence), each verification command's real result, new head SHA, finding-resolve outcome. If anything failed, say so plainly with the output — do not report success you did not observe.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85/tasks/af35f1ec41f89ea32.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"431660b2-bc0c-43cc-9193-ecb27138e4be","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":255},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibilit